<concept id="concept-4608" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic concept/concept "><title class="- topic/title ">Certificate Use case for OPC UA</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This topic explains how you might choose to use the Workbench views to generate certificates or when you might choose to use the script method for certificate generation, based on your use case.</shortdesc><conbody class="- topic/body  concept/conbody "><p class="- topic/p ">Refer to the information below:</p><table class="- topic/table "><tgroup cols="3" class="- topic/tgroup "><colspec colname="c1" colnum="1" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="c2" colnum="2" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="c3" colnum="3" class="- topic/colspec "/><thead class="- topic/thead "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">
                            <p class="- topic/p "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">Use Case</b></p>
                        </entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">
                            <p class="- topic/p "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">Method</b></p>
                        </entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">
                            <p class="- topic/p "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">When to Use</b></p>
                        </entry></row></thead><tbody class="- topic/tbody "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">Standard server setup</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Use <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword "/> Certificate Management </entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Most common scenarios of generating a certificate for OPC UA cert auth/Signing+Encryption. Easier setup and recommended.</entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">Integration with existing PKI</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">External tools</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">When you need specific certificate formats, CA signing, or integration with enterprise certificate management. However, you can still generate certificate using the Workbench view and export the certificate.</entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">Automated deployment</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">External tools</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">For scripted/automated certificate provisioning.</entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table><note class="- topic/note ">You can generate a certificate using various tools, but the most effective approach is to use the <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword "/> Certificate Management..</note></conbody></concept>